      "name": null,
      "problem": "Use the first four terms of the binomial expansion of $(1+x)^{9}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(0.92)^{9}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n$(0.92)^{9}≈$ \n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that when $n$ is a positive integer, \n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{1}{2!}n(n-1){x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3!}n(n-1)(n-2){x}^{3}+⋯+{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+x)}^{9} & =1+9x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot {x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot {x}^{3}+⋯+{x}^{9} \\\\  & =1+9x+36{x}^{2}+84{x}^{3}+⋯\\,+{x}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{9}≈1+9x+36{x}^{2}+84{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.08$ into the above approximation of $(1+x)^{9}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0.92)^{9} & =(1+(-0.08))^{9} \\\\  & ≈1+9(-0.08)+36(-0.08)^{2}+84(-0.08)^{3} \\\\  & =1-9(0.08)+36(0.006\\,4)-84(0.000\\,512) \\\\  & =1-0.72+0.2304-0.043\\,008 \\\\  & ≈0.467\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
